<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="u1a-ct-labeled">
  <title>Unit 1a Subgoal Labeled Puzzles for Toggle Code</title>
  <p>
    These are copies of the Mixed Up Code Practice 1a puzzles with subgoal
    labels added. The Unit 1a Toggle Code Practice page uses them as the Get
    Help puzzles for its write code problems. Problems whose solution has
    fewer than two subgoals keep the original, unlabeled puzzle.
  </p>

  <activity label="u1aex4muc-sgl" xml:id="u1aex4muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="hide" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The following program segment should figure out the cost for each shirt
        if they are buy 2 and get the third free and they are originally $45
        each. But, the blocks have been mixed up. Drag the blocks from the left
        and put them in the correct order on the right. Click the Check button
        to check your solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="2">
        <cline>// Store the original price per shirt</cline>
        <cline>double price = 45;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="1">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>// Find the total paid for three shirts</cline>
          <cline>double totalCost = price * 2;</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>// Find the total paid for three shirts</cline>
          <cline>double totalCost = price * 3;</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="3">
        <cline>// Split the total paid equally among the shirts</cline>
        <cline>double pricePerShirt = totalCost / 3;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="4">
        <cline>// Display the cost per shirt</cline>
        <cline>System.out.println(pricePerShirt);</cline>
      </block>
    </blocks>
  </activity>

  <activity label="u1aex5muc-sgl" xml:id="u1aex5muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="hide" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The following program segment should figure out the cost per person for
        a dinner including the tip. But the blocks have been mixed up and may
        include an extra block that isn’t needed in the solution. Drag the
        needed blocks from the left and put them in the correct order on the
        right. Click the Check button to check your solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="1">
        <cline>// Store the bill</cline>
        <cline>double bill = 89.23;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="5">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>// Find the tip as a percent of the bill</cline>
          <cline>double tip = bill * 0.20;</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>// Find the tip as a percent of the bill</cline>
          <cline>double tip = bill * 20;</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="4">
        <cline>// Raise the bill by the tip</cline>
        <cline>double total = bill + tip;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="3">
        <cline>// Split the total equally among the people</cline>
        <cline>double perPersonCost = total / 3;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="2">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>// Display the cost per person</cline>
          <cline>System.out.println(perPersonCost);</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>// Display the cost per person</cline>
          <cline>System.out.println(perpersoncost);</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>
    </blocks>
  </activity>

  <activity label="u1aex6muc-sgl" xml:id="u1aex6muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="hide" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The main method in the following class should print the number of
        seconds in 5 days. But, the blocks have been mixed up and may include an
        extra block that isn’t needed in the solution. Drag the needed blocks
        from the left and put them in the correct order on the right. Click the
        Check button to check your solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="9">
        <cline>public class Test1</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="4">
        <cline>    public static void main(String[] args)</cline>
        <cline>    {</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="7">
        <cline>        // Store the time conversion rates</cline>
        <cline>        int sInMin = 60;</cline>
        <cline>        int mInHour = 60;</cline>
        <cline>        int hInDay = 24;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="2">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Combine the rates into seconds per day</cline>
          <cline>        int sInDay = sInMin * mInHour * hInDay;</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Combine the rates into seconds per day</cline>
          <cline>        int sInDay = sInMin + mInHour + hInDay;</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="5">
        <cline>        // Use a rate to change days to seconds</cline>
        <cline>        int total = sInDay * 5;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="8">
        <cline>        // Display the number of seconds</cline>
        <cline>        System.out.println(total);</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="3">
        <cline>    } // end main method</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="6">
        <cline>} // end of class</cline>
      </block>

    </blocks>
  </activity>

  <activity label="u1aex7muc-sgl" xml:id="u1aex7muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="hide" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The main method in the following class should calculate the number of
        months it would take you to save 500 if you make 50 a week. But, the
        blocks have been mixed up and may include an extra block that isn’t
        needed in the solution. Drag the needed blocks from the left and put
        them in the correct order on the right. Click the Check button to check
        your solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="8">
        <cline>public class Test1</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="4">
        <cline>    public static void main(String[] args)</cline>
        <cline>    {</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="6">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Store the savings goal, weekly pay, and weeks per month</cline>
          <cline>        double weeklyRate = 50;</cline>
          <cline>        double goal = 500;</cline>
          <cline>        double weeksPerMonth = 4;</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Store the savings goal, weekly pay, and weeks per month</cline>
          <cline>        int weeklyRate = 50;</cline>
          <cline>        int goal = 500;</cline>
          <cline>        int weeksPerMonth = 4;</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="3">
        <cline>        // Use a rate to change dollars to weeks</cline>
        <cline>        double numWeeks = goal / weeklyRate;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="1">
        <cline>        // Use a rate to change weeks to months</cline>
        <cline>        double numMonths = numWeeks / weeksPerMonth;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="2">
        <cline>        // Display the number of months</cline>
        <cline>        System.out.println(numMonths);</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="7">
        <cline>    } // end main method</cline>
        <cline>} // end of class</cline>
      </block>

    </blocks>
  </activity>

  <activity label="u1aex10muc-sgl" xml:id="u1aex10muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="hide" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The main method in the following class should calculate the cost of a
        trip that is 200 miles when the price of gas is 2.20 and the miles per
        gallon is 42. But, the blocks have been mixed up and may include an
        extra block that isn’t needed in the solution. Drag the needed blocks
        from the left and put them in the correct order on the right. Click the
        Check button to check your solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="1">
        <cline>public class Test1</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="2">
        <cline>    public static void main(String[] args)</cline>
        <cline>    {</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="7">
        <cline>        // Store the trip distance, gas price, and miles per gallon</cline>
        <cline>        int miles = 200;</cline>
        <cline>        double price = 2.20;</cline>
        <cline>        int mpg = 42;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="6">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Use a rate to change miles to gallons</cline>
          <cline>        double numGalls = (double) miles / mpg;</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Use a rate to change miles to gallons</cline>
          <cline>        double numGalls = (double) (miles / mpg);</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="9">
        <cline>        // Use a rate to change gallons to dollars</cline>
        <cline>        double totalCost = numGalls * price;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="10">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Display the cost of the trip</cline>
          <cline>        System.out.println(totalCost);</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Display the cost of the trip</cline>
          <cline>        System.println(totalCost);</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="8">
        <cline>    } // end main method</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="4">
        <cline>} // end of class</cline>
      </block>
    </blocks>
  </activity>

  <activity label="u1aex11muc-sgl" xml:id="u1aex11muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="hide" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The main method in the following class should calculate how many miles
        you can go on half a tank of gas if the miles per gallon is 26 and your
        tank holds 15 gallons. But, the blocks have been mixed up and may
        include an extra block that isn’t needed in the solution. Drag the
        needed blocks from the left and put them in the correct order on the
        right. Click the Check button to check your solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="1">
        <cline>public class Test1</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="2">
        <cline>    public static void main(String[] args)</cline>
        <cline>    {</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="5">
        <cline>        // Store the miles per gallon and the tank size</cline>
        <cline>        int mpg = 26;</cline>
        <cline>        int tankHolds = 15;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="7">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Find the gallons in half a tank</cline>
          <cline>        double numGalls = (double) tankHolds / 2;</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Find the gallons in half a tank</cline>
          <cline>        double numGalls = tankHolds / 2;</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="10">
        <cline>        // Use a rate to change gallons to miles</cline>
        <cline>        double miles = numGalls * mpg;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="8">
        <cline>        // Display the miles you can go</cline>
        <cline>        System.out.println(miles);</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="6">
        <cline>    } // end main method</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="9">
        <cline>} // end of class</cline>
      </block>

    </blocks>
  </activity>

  <activity label="u1aex12muc-sgl" xml:id="u1aex12muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="hide" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The main method in the following class should calculate how many chicken
        wings you can buy with $3.50 if the wings are $.60 each. But, the blocks
        have been mixed up and may include an extra block that isn’t needed in
        the solution. Drag the needed blocks from the left and put them in the
        correct order on the right. Click the Check button to check your
        solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="2">
        <cline>public class Test1</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="1">
        <cline>    public static void main(String[] args)</cline>
        <cline>    {</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="8">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Store the money you have and the price per wing</cline>
          <cline>        double cost = 0.6;</cline>
          <cline>        double money = 3.5;</cline>
        </choice>

        <choice>
          <cline>        // Store the money you have and the price per wing</cline>
          <cline>        int cost = 0.6;</cline>
          <cline>        int money = 3.5;</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="9">
        <cline>        // Use a rate to change dollars to wings</cline>
        <cline>        double exactWings = money / cost;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="10">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Convert the number of wings to an integer</cline>
          <cline>        int numWings = (int) exactWings;</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Convert the number of wings to an integer</cline>
          <cline>        int numWings = exactWings;</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="7">
        <cline>        // Display the number of wings</cline>
        <cline>        System.out.println(numWings);</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="3">
        <cline>    } // end main method</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="6">
        <cline>} // end of class</cline>
      </block>
    </blocks>
  </activity>

  <activity label="u1aex13muc-sgl" xml:id="u1aex13muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="hide" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The main method in the following class should calculate how much you
        will have to pay for an item that is 60% off the original price of
        $52.99. But, the blocks have been mixed up and may include an extra
        block that isn’t needed in the solution. Drag the needed blocks from the
        left and put them in the correct order on the right. Click the Check
        button to check your solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="8">
        <cline>public class Test1</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="4">
        <cline>    public static void main(String[] args)</cline>
        <cline>    {</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="6">
        <cline>        // Store the original price and the percent off</cline>
        <cline>        double price = 52.99;</cline>
        <cline>        double discount = 0.6;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="10">
        <cline>        // Find the savings as a percent of the price</cline>
        <cline>        double savings = price * discount;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="5">
        <cline>        // Lower the original price by the savings</cline>
        <cline>        double finalPrice = price - savings;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="9">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Display the price you pay</cline>
          <cline>        System.out.println(finalPrice);</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Display the price you pay</cline>
          <cline>        System.out.println(savings);</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="3">
        <cline>    } // end main method</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="7">
        <cline>} // end of class</cline>
      </block>

    </blocks>
  </activity>

  <activity label="u1aex14muc-sgl" xml:id="u1aex14muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="hide" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The main method in the following class should calculate how much the per
        item costs is for shorts that are buy 2 and get the third free. The
        shorts are $39.99 each. But, the blocks have been mixed up and may
        include an extra block that isn’t needed in the solution. Drag the
        needed blocks from the left and put them in the correct order on the
        right. Click the Check button to check your solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="5">
        <cline>public class Test1</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="2">
        <cline>    public static void main(String[] args)</cline>
        <cline>    {</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="1">
        <cline>        // Store the original price per pair of shorts</cline>
        <cline>        double price = 39.99;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="6">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Find the total paid for three pairs of shorts</cline>
          <cline>        double priceForTwo = price * 2;</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Find the total paid for three pairs of shorts</cline>
          <cline>        double priceForTwo = price * 2</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="3">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Split the total paid equally among the shorts</cline>
          <cline>        double itemPrice = priceForTwo / 3;</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Split the total paid equally among the shorts</cline>
          <cline>        double itemPrice = priceForTwo / 2;</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="10">
        <cline>        // Display the cost per pair of shorts</cline>
        <cline>        System.out.println(itemPrice);</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="9">
        <cline>    } // end main method</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="7">
        <cline>} // end of class</cline>
      </block>
    </blocks>
  </activity>
</section>
